{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1196727-so-do-they-just-not-acknowledge-leprechauns-as-a-thing","id":1196727,"title":"So do they just not acknowledge leprechauns as a Thing?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-17T23:19:50-07:00","id":1196727,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> So do they just not acknowledge leprechauns as a Thing?","content":"So now that its no longer Saint Patty's day I'm celebrating late. I always loved the Clarichauns but something bothers me. Is it they just say nope mortals got it wrong there weren't Leprachauns and Clarichauns, only Clarichauns? It feels to me back in the day they did the Clarichaun thing because its an edgier cooler less known fae, like using Redcaps instead of Goblins (though we later got Goblins who I would have liked if they called them Gremlins instead...). Were Leprachauns never a thing? If feels to me it would have been more cohesive if they did Leprachauns were the Kith, and Clarichauns the Thallain. Now don't get me wrong I love how they did it, both Clarichauns and Bodhachs. Just addressing the Green Elephant in the room.<br /> <br /> I know they wanted to differentiate them more from Boggans and make them more exciting/romantic but it would have been neat to keep a bit more of their tradition as cobblers of shoes and maybe be brewing experts too.<br /> <br /> Just felt the Clarichaun pick in C20 was trying to be too edgy by making it a tall looking guy who didn't really wear much green. I would have kept the green thing as a highlight, like how Redcaps treat red.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T00:39:18-07:00","id":1196734,"title":"","content":"Whether or not Clurichaun and leprchauns are separate concepts of just regional variations on the same fairy is an argument that professional folklorist have been arguing for centuries. While the gamer in us probably wants a neat setup of various &quot;-chaun&quot; types each with theirown splat and specialization, folklore is rarely so neat and tidy so one could easily decide Clurichaun are the real kith, especially since Leprechaun has.. baggage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T01:40:38-07:00","id":1196741,"title":"","content":"Yeah I figure they ditched it because of the baggage, for the same reason they chose Sidhe as a kith instead of say elf/alfar. But it seems unavoidable to ignore Leprachaun in the discussion. So either its something that would cause the Clarichaun to laugh/be furious or its something they go by half the time which is probably how I would handle it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T12:40:32-07:00","id":1196876,"title":"","content":"I'm reminded of this:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://imgflip.com/i/1q4lrx\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://i.imgflip.com/1q4lrx.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><a href=\"https://imgflip.com/memegenerator\" target=\"_blank\">via Imgflip Meme Generator</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T15:13:50-07:00","id":1196915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1196727-so-do-they-just-not-acknowledge-leprechauns-as-a-thing?p=1196741#post1196741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I figure they ditched it because of the baggage, for the same reason they chose Sidhe as a kith instead of say elf/alfar. But it seems unavoidable to ignore Leprachaun in the discussion. So either its something that would cause the Clarichaun to laugh/be furious or its something they go by half the time which is probably how I would handle it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems as avoidable as elf/Alfar. I mean no one asks Sidhe if they are that or Leyshey or whatever..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T05:34:33-07:00","id":1197142,"title":"","content":"You've also got to factor in self-identity. People often choose names because they want to avoid the baggage that might come with another, more popularly used name. I could see the politics behind the names being a large driver of that terminology. The kith has scope to represent both versions of the myth, still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T05:45:53-07:00","id":1197146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1196727-so-do-they-just-not-acknowledge-leprechauns-as-a-thing?p=1197142#post1197142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've also got to factor in self-identity. People often choose names because they want to avoid the baggage that might come with another, more popularly used name. I could see the politics behind the names being a large driver of that terminology. The kith has scope to represent both versions of the myth, still.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then what about over a hundred years ago, before mass media, Darby O'gill, and Lucky Charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T06:59:33-07:00","id":1197172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1196727-so-do-they-just-not-acknowledge-leprechauns-as-a-thing?p=1197146#post1197146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then what about over a hundred years ago, before mass media, Darby O'gill, and Lucky Charms?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What do you think Pooka were called 100 years ago? Do you think they are called Pooka all kithaindom?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T13:36:14-07:00","id":1197315,"title":"","content":"I prefer Leprechauns. Clarichaun in the Hood just doesn't roll off the tongue quite as well. <br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/tY1D90ng0kE/movieposter.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T14:00:47-07:00","id":1197322,"title":"","content":"Nitpick incoming: The shortened form of Patrick (at least in Ireland) is Paddy. Patty is short for Patricia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T14:58:03-07:00","id":1197341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1196727-so-do-they-just-not-acknowledge-leprechauns-as-a-thing?p=1197322#post1197322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nitpick incoming: The shortened form of Patrick (at least in Ireland) is Paddy. Patty is short for Patricia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Comhghairdeas leat, a Willow!<br /> <br /> The reasoning is fairly simple. Patrick isn't an Irish name, but P\u00e1draig is. So it's shortened to Paddy when referring to the name P\u00e1draig, which most people just say as Patrick in English. <br /> <br /> Sl\u00e1n.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11658-rabbit-pooka","name":"Rabbit Pooka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11658_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T15:10:43-07:00","id":1197347,"title":"","content":"Exactly hence why Pat and Patty are neutral gender names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T04:36:24-07:00","id":1199656,"title":"","content":"Check the Court off All Kings (novel) pg. 151. Leprechaun is just the degenerated human name of Chlurichauns and nothing more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T19:08:26-07:00","id":1199912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rabbit Pooka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1196727-so-do-they-just-not-acknowledge-leprechauns-as-a-thing?p=1197341#post1197341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Comhghairdeas leat, a Willow!</div> </div> </div> </div>A Bhuileo* (D\u00e1 mba an Ghaelainn ghlan a theasta\u00edonn uait <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> *To anybody reading that'd be Willow in Gaelic spelling, bit in brackets basically means &quot;If you want to be a purist&quot; as a joke","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T04:29:51-07:00","id":1207932,"title":"","content":"Something else bothering me... the Clarichauns are the only Kith without pointed Ears in the kith section... and they really don't even have a fae mien...<br /> <br /> So at the very least I am going to have them have pointed ears. And a possibly apocryphal origin of them being degenerated sidhe, since their origins in the real world are essentially the folklorization of the Tuatha gods of Ireland. So a batch of Sidhe degenerated into Clarichaun upontaking up the Changeling Way ritual and dying. They were reborn into Clarichaun and lost their Houses.<br /> <br /> At least this way the Clarichaun would be something akin to commoner/nonsuper beautiful Sidhe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T04:37:42-07:00","id":1207933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1196727-so-do-they-just-not-acknowledge-leprechauns-as-a-thing?p=1207932#post1207932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something else bothering me... the Clarichauns are the only Kith without pointed Ears in the kith section... .</div> </div> </div> </div>Sluagh have no ears!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}